OpenRSP in VibeServer.app
=========================

This app contains OpenRSP, an independent, open-source driver stack for RSP-family receivers
(https://openrsp.dev), so that an RSP works with VibeServer with nothing else installed:

  Contents/Frameworks/libsdrplay_api.so.3.15        the API library VibeServer loads
  Contents/MacOS/vibeserver-rspd                     the device service, run by the app while it is open
  Contents/Resources/openrsp/firmware/own/           OpenRSP's USB bridge firmware

OpenRSP is not made, endorsed or supported by SDRplay Ltd. Please report problems with it to the VibeSDR
project, not to SDRplay. Copyright (C) 2026 the OpenRSP authors. It is free software under the GNU General
Public License, version 3 or later: see Contents/Resources/COPYING.openrsp.

Source code
-----------
The Corresponding Source of these files is the directory vendor/openrsp of the VibeSDR source code, at the
release tag matching this app's version: https://github.com/Stuey3D/VibeSDR
It is OpenRSP 3.15.2-20 (https://openrsp.dev/downloads/openrsp-3.15.2-20-src.tar.gz, SHA-256
288828d04beb4ecb0812ee8a3635b31b539c9b1b4dbb4344e2f127fd6ec20057) with the build changes listed in
VIBESDR-CHANGES beside this file. vibeserver/mac/build-app.sh (section "OpenRSP") shows how it is built;
the firmware images are vendor/openrsp-firmware (see its README).

If an SDRplay API is already installed
--------------------------------------
If SDRplay's own API is installed (/Library/SDRplayAPI, with its launch daemon), that installation keeps
the receivers for every program on this Mac: VibeServer does not start its own service, and uses the
installed library. Nothing of it is changed or removed. Uninstall it to use the driver in this app instead.
